Usage example:

```tsx
// Example parent usage
<CheckoutScreen
  items={cartItems}
  currency="USD"
  deliveryFee={4.99}
  isSubmitting={isPaying}
  onBack={() => navigate('/cart')}
  onPay={(address) => submitOrder(cartItems, address)}
/>
```

Notes on key decisions:
- The native Telegram `BackButton` and `MainButton` are wired up via the WebApp SDK, with a fallback in-page Pay button that only renders when `window.Telegram.WebApp` isn't present (e.g. during local dev in a plain browser).
- Theme colors use Telegram's CSS variables (`--tg-theme-*`) with light-mode fallbacks, so it adapts to the user's Telegram theme automatically if those variables are set on `:root` by your app's bootstrap code.
- Validation is simple client-side required/format checks; wire `onPay` to your real payment flow (e.g. Telegram Payments invoice or your backend).
